tel 1.0

# The header of a Fever script (lira's fury.md §12a and fever.md §6a): the TEL document before
# the `##` line that separates it from the Scala source. The vocabulary is Fury's, so that the
# same file runs under `fury` unchanged; this base is deliberately small, and `include` (lira
# coordinates), `require`, `artifact` and JVM options arrive as layers, each a TEL subtype step
# rather than a revision. Unknown keys are refused: everything that reaches the compiler must be
# declared and hashable (builds.md §3.1).

name fever-script

scalar Form
  description
      The source form of the body. Fever compiles `scala` alone; another form is an error naming
      it.
  pattern scala

scalar ScalacFlag
  description
      One scalac command-line flag, verbatim, e.g. -deprecation or -Wunused:imports.
  pattern -.*

scalar ClasspathEntry
  description
      A jar or class directory for the body's compile and run classpath, resolved against the
      script's own directory unless absolute.
  validate string

record Language
  description
      The body's source form, with the compiler options for it beneath.

  field form Form
  field flag ScalacFlag optional repeatable

document
  field language Language
  field classpath ClasspathEntry optional repeatable
